<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <!--
        The Accountant agent, as a ROSTER ENTRY only.

        Requested by the owner 2026-09-07 after reviewing the Agent Profiles
        list. It is created here, visible and configured, and it holds **no
        tools and no model permissions at all**.

        That is not an oversight, and it is not laziness. Document B 1 puts
        Sales, Finance, HR and General Manager agents out of Phase 1 and says
        their data "exists in the database purely as isolation targets". Doc B
        11's sharp-edge note is more specific still: the figure a Finance Agent
        would report "requires a Finance Agent that does not exist in Phase 1,
        and even in Phase 2 it will require an explicit handoff type."

        Granting this profile account.move would not be an addition, it would be
        a subtraction from the thing the platform is sold on:

          - 11 row 1  Procurement asked for net profit -> refusal
          - 11 row 2  the same with the system prompt rewritten -> THE GO/NO-GO
          - 11 row 4  Quality asked the value of affected shipments -> refusal
          - 13 X-04   posted account.move exists SO THAT it can be refused
          - 15        "Every isolation proof in 11 passes" is Phase 1 acceptance

        So the agent exists, is configured, and can do nothing. Giving it scope
        is a Phase 2 decision that changes Document B and needs the owner's
        sign-off, not a configuration change.
    -->
    <record id="profile_accounting" model="ai.operations.agent.profile">
        <field name="name">Accounting Intelligence</field>
        <field name="code">accounting</field>
        <field name="active" eval="False"/>
        <field name="max_autonomy_level">0</field>
        <field name="policy_version">1.0.0</field>
        <field name="description">Financial reporting and analysis. PHASE 2:
            this agent holds no tools and no model permissions in Phase 1. The
            accounting data in this database exists so that the other four
            agents can be refused it; see Document B section 11.</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
